WEBVTT

00:00:00.082 --> 00:00:03.416
Osimertinib, also called Tagrisso, is a daily tablet

00:00:03.416 --> 00:00:06.492
for certain types of non-small cell lung cancer.

00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:11.872
A change in a gene called EGFR can keep telling cancer cells to grow.

00:00:12.242 --> 00:00:13.892
This medicine blocks that signal.

00:00:14.202 --> 00:00:17.252
A test on your cancer helps your team decide if it is right for you.

00:00:17.662 --> 00:00:20.022
After surgery, you may take it for up to three years

00:00:20.022 --> 00:00:21.972
to reduce the chance of cancer coming back.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.554
For advanced cancer, treatment usually continues

00:00:24.554 --> 00:00:26.972
while it is helping and side effects are manageable.

00:00:27.222 --> 00:00:29.612
The usual dose is 80 mg once a day.

00:00:29.902 --> 00:00:34.032
Take your prescribed dose at about the same time each day, with or without food.

00:00:34.362 --> 00:00:35.932
There is no planned week off.

00:00:36.242 --> 00:00:38.072
Swallow the tablet whole with water.

00:00:38.382 --> 00:00:42.032
If swallowing is difficult, ask your pharmacist how to disperse it safely.

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:46.555
If you miss a dose, take it if your next dose is more than 12 hours away.

00:00:46.965 --> 00:00:49.475
If fewer than 12 hours remain, skip it.

00:00:49.905 --> 00:00:52.895
At exactly 12 hours, ask your pharmacist.

00:00:53.225 --> 00:00:54.115
Never double up.

00:00:54.445 --> 00:00:56.515
Check new medicines with your pharmacist.

00:00:56.945 --> 00:00:58.235
Avoid St John’s wort.

00:00:58.526 --> 00:01:01.347
Your team will check your blood and check your heart rhythm.

00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:09.679
Loose stools, rash, dry skin, mouth ulcers and sore nails are common.

00:01:10.289 --> 00:01:13.759
Ring your team if diarrhoea persists or you struggle to drink.

00:01:14.232 --> 00:01:17.477
Ring your 24-hour oncology line straight away for a new

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:20.074
or worsening cough, breathlessness or fever.

00:01:20.504 --> 00:01:22.294
These can be signs of lung inflammation.

00:01:22.664 --> 00:01:26.194
Also call urgently for blistering skin or a painful red eye.

00:01:26.526 --> 00:01:30.857
Tell your team urgently about a racing heartbeat, fainting or changes in your eyesight.

00:01:31.346 --> 00:01:35.476
If you feel unwell and cannot reach oncology, seek urgent medical assessment.

00:01:35.866 --> 00:01:38.512
For severe breathing difficulty, severe chest pain

00:01:38.512 --> 00:01:40.576
or collapse, call 112 for an ambulance.
